Subject: Cantor EVO-X2 Plan-Only Build Job P0 Justification

@ [justification_uuid] 39dcce8b-19c7-4f84-ac50-30834f8449e0
@ [canonical_uuid] 3482e2ce-817c-4788-b185-35adaad414f7

& [WhyNow]
  + EVO-X2 already hosts exact current Cantor binaries and passes deterministic replay, so the next smallest product-learning step is to make Cantor produce a current build work object there

& [WhyPlanOnly]
  + source transfer workspace creation toolchain validation Cargo execution and performance measurement each introduce distinct authority failure and rollback surfaces
  + combining them would make success and failure ambiguous and could confuse a generated plan with permission to act

& [WhyTypedAndDeterministic]
  + closed shapes exact digests inert atoms and independent recompilation make drift authority promotion and noncanonical input observable
  + fresh-process equality tests the intended host behavior without hidden custody

& [WhyThisRoot]
  + a new immutable isolated root preserves the completed P0 deployment and all historical services while giving the planner an exact rollback boundary

& [Decision]
  + authorize formation and after publication a provider-free local implementation only; remote execution and physical build effects remain separately gated
